Creating a first-person controller script in Godot Engine involves writing a script that can handle input, update the camera position, and apply the appropriate transformations to your character (KinematicBody). Here's a basic example of a first-person controller script for Godot Engine 3.x:

```gdscript
extends KinematicBody

var speed = 200.0
var gravity = 500.0

func _physics_process(delta):
    var direction = Vector3.ZERO

    if Input.is_action_just_pressed("move_left"):
        direction.x -= 1
    if Input.is_action_just_pressed("move_right"):
        direction.x += 1
    if Input.is_action_just_pressed("move_forward"):
        direction.y -= 1
    if Input.is_action_just_pressed("move_backward"):
        direction.y += 1

    direction = direction.normalized() * speed

    if is_on_floor():
        direction.y -= gravity * delta

