public class PowerOfThree {

    public static boolean isPowerOfThree(int n) {
        if (n <= 0) {
            return false;
        }
        int exponent = 1;
        while (exponent < n) {
            exponent *= 3;
        }
        return n == exponent;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println(isPowerOfThree(27)); // true
        System.out.println(isPowerOfThree(0));  // false
        System.out.println(isPowerOfThree(-1)); // false
    }
}
```

This code checks if `n` is a power of three by continuously multiplying 3 by itself until it either matches `n` (which means `n` is a power of three) or surpasses `n` (which means `n` is not a power of three).

